{%- comment -%}
  INSTALLATION EDIT for sections/header.liquid (Dawn)

  1. SAVE the file snippets/header-kebab-menu.liquid into your theme
     (Online Store > Themes > Edit code > Add a new snippet).

  2. IN sections/header.liquid, FIND the existing hamburger button.
     It looks like this (Dawn 15.x):

       <details id="Details-menu-drawer-container" class="menu-drawer-container">
         <summary class="header__icon header__icon--menu header__icon--summary link focus-inset" ...>
           <span>
             {%- render 'icon-hamburger' -%}
             {%- render 'icon-close' -%}
           </span>
         </summary>
       ...

  3. REPLACE the <span>…icon-hamburger…icon-close…</span> inside that
     <summary> with the kebab snippet render, OR (cleaner) replace the
     whole <summary> block with:

       {% render 'header-kebab-menu' %}

     and remove the now-unused <details>/<summary> drawer trigger.

  4. HIDE the original drawer panel on mobile by adding this rule to
     kebab-menu.css (already included at the bottom of that file if you
     prefer, otherwise paste here):

       @media screen and (max-width: 749.98px) {
         .header__icon--menu,
         .header__icon--menu + .header__drawer,
         #menu-drawer,
         .menu-drawer,
         .header__drawer {
           display: none !important;
         }
       }

     (Only needed if you keep the old <details> markup around; if you
      fully replace the <summary> with {% render 'header-kebab-menu' %},
      none of this hiding is necessary.)

  5. MAKE SURE the parent wrapper of the kebab toggle has
     position: relative and sits inside the left-side header icon
     group so it lines up exactly where the hamburger used to sit.

  6. LOAD the CSS — add this to layout/theme.liquid right before the
     </head> (or append to assets/base.css, but a separate file is
     cleaner to remove later):

       <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'kebab-menu.css' | asset_url }}">

     Then upload kebab-menu.css as a new asset.

  7. LOAD the JS — add this right before </body> in layout/theme.liquid:

       <script src="{{ 'kebab-menu.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

     Then upload kebab-menu.js as a new asset. Deferred so it runs
     after Dawn's own JS; no conflict since everything is scoped to
     [data-mg-kebab].

  8. DONE. Menu items (All products, Love, Birthday Gifts, Occasions,
     Relationship, Corporate, Greetings, My Orders) are read live from
     Admin > Navigation > main-menu. Edit them there — no code change
     needed. The active page is auto-highlighted via link.active.
{%- endcomment -%}
